WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.350
You have often asked why in a channel called
VisualPolitik we sometimes make videos about

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.350
companies.

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:09.190
For example, we already talked about, Amazon,
Inditex and Tesla, among others.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:12.060
Well, we do it for two fundamental reasons:

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:16.480
The first one is that we see politics in a
broad sense, that is, we can’t talk about

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.730
politics without considering economic and
social issues.

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:23.830
And, of course, I don’t think we can deny
the huge influence that big companies have

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:27.060
in our lives today.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:33.050
Secondly, we know that many of you also love
these kinds of videos so we keep making them.

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:34.050
And, you know what?

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:35.300
We like these kinds of subjects too…

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.300
so…

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.300
here we go.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:51.539
In this video, we have a pretty interesting
combination: BMW, Germany and China.

00:00:51.539 --> 00:00:55.890
As we mentioned here at VisualPolitik, Germany
is the mother factory of the world.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.559
The country where machines and the things
that go into the things that other countries

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:03.940
produce are manufactured.

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:08.549
And of course, of all industries, the automobile
industry is, without a doubt, the most famous

00:01:08.549 --> 00:01:10.450
and most peculiar.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:18.130
We all know that brands like Mercedes, BMW,
Volkswagen, Porsche, Opel and Audi are German.

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:22.390
And this is because Germany isn’t only one
of the largest car producers in the world,

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:26.180
it is also considered the cradle of the first
car.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:28.850
You heard that right.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:35.810
In 1885, an engineer called Karl Benz, tried
to place a combustion engine into a three-wheeled

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:36.810
chariot:

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:42.070
This was known as the Benz Patent-Motorwagen
and was able to reach the astounding speed

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:46.240
of 16km per hour.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:53.049
In total, 25 units were manufactured and in
one of them, Bertha Benz, Karl Benz’s wife,

00:01:53.049 --> 00:01:57.640
made what is considered the first car trip
in history, for a distance of actually 94

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:01.250
km, which isn’t bad
By the way, have you noticed something?

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:03.590
Back then, there were of course no gas stations...

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:06.390
so how did Bertha Benz refuel?

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:10.070
Well, by buying a petroleum derivative in
pharmacies, ether.

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:14.900
Yes, that's right, we could say that pharmacies
were the first gas stations in history.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:20.950
But... of course, that's not the reason why
cars in Germany are so important.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:28.240
You see, because more machines are always
needed, the automotive industry, my friends,

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:31.050
is one of the most productive and most capitalized..

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:35.590
So… what better place to manufacture them
than Germany, the country of machines?

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:36.590
However...

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:41.260
despite this... let's just say that in recent
times the German automotive industry, and

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:48.380
the European automotive industry in general,
hasn’t been the most popular one.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:55.230
(IN DANGER OF EXTINCTION?)

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:59.600
In recent times there has been a widespread
feeling that the traditional automotive industry,

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:05.370
and especially as we said European manufacturers,
will be the big losers of the upcoming electric

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:08.500
car and autonomous car revolution.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:15.260
Because, who would want one of those old companies
when we have fresh and innovative companies

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:18.640
like Tesla?

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:23.880
I talked about it here, on VisualPolitik,
not so long ago.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:27.650
Despite never having made money and producing
very few cars, Tesla has a market value that

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:34.080
is as large as that of BMW and which is far
superior to companies such as Renault or Peugeot.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.540
How is this possible?

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:42.620
Well as we saw, basically because many investors
consider that in a few years, Tesla will literally

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:43.720
take over the market.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:47.180
And here, my friends, is where some questions
arise:

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:49.460
Will the electric car transition really be
that quick?

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:54.190
Are European manufacturers too late to join
this revolution?

00:03:54.190 --> 00:04:02.570
I don’t know what you think, but some information
at least doesn’t seem to support these ideas.

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:03.570
See:

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:08.350
"According to a recent study from the IFO
Institute, Europe owns almost half of all

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:12.770
patents related to the electric car, leading
the world ranking, and being well ahead of

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:16.530
countries such as Japan (23%) and the United
States (18%)."

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:25.360
Iván Martín, President and Chief Investment
Officer of Magallanes Value Investors.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:33.350
Well, let's assume that Elon Musk is right,
and Tesla manages to overcome all the problems

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:37.490
that currently affect it - for example, the
production of Model 3 – and thus fulfills

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:42.310
his most ambitious forecasts, managing to
sell 2 million cars in 2022.

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:46.640
This means that he would have to multiply
his production capacity not by 2 or by 5,

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:49.780
but by 20 in just over 4 years.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:54.960
Well, in that same year, at least 110 million
vehicles are expected to be produced in the

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.380
world.

00:04:57.380 --> 00:05:05.250
Honestly, considering the strong growth of
the middle class in emerging markets, I would

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:08.130
bet on far more vehicle production than that,
but...

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:10.620
OK, let's be prudent and stay with that number

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:16.350
Out of those 110 million cars, no more than
20% are expected to be electric cars or plug-in

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:17.350
hybrids

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.970
So, what would that mean?…

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:23.310
well, that in the best case scenario, Tesla
would have a market share in the industry

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:25.930
of less than 2%, and 9% in the electric car
market.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:40.850
In other words, my friends, we could say that
the cards aren’t dealt yet and that even

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:46.160
if Tesla's best forecasts are met, there will
be many more companies in the market... companies

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:49.430
such as BMW.

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:56.460
(A GERMAN ICON)

00:05:56.460 --> 00:06:01.800
BMW is one of the great icons of the German
industry.

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:05.960
Robust, luxurious and technologically advanced
cars.

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:11.840
Who doesn’t want a BMW?

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:17.770
See, in 9 of the past 10 years, this brand
has been the world leader in premium cars.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:20.240
And the truth is, my friends, that this is
quite interesting.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:25.570
See, this company, besides owning BMW, also
owns Mini and Rolls Royce, and at the time

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:29.840
of publishing this video has a market value
that is very similar to that of Tesla, about

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:31.250
50 billion dollars.

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:37.630
Despite this... both companies have many,
many differences.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:44.830
While in 2016 Elon Musk’s company managed
to sell 76,000 cars while losing 770 million

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:50.889
dollars; the German company sold 2,360,000
cars and had a profit after tax of more than

00:06:50.889 --> 00:06:52.710
7 billion dollars.

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:57.190
Yes, I know, some of you may now be thinking:

00:06:57.190 --> 00:07:01.530
Wait, wait, Simon, this isn’t a fair comparison,
Tesla is currently investing in research and

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:05.560
developing new technologies; while BMW makes
the same cars they’ve been making since

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:06.560
the beginning.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:09.490
Well, it isn’t quite like that:

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:15.710
In 2016, for example, the German group invested
more than $ 5 billion in research and development.

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:20.860
Meanwhile, Tesla's investment was 5 times
smaller, slightly less than $ 1 billion.

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:24.110
And, of course, a lot of that investment is
going, where?

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:28.550
To develop electric and autonomous models.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:34.420
“BMW to spend $237 million on battery cell
center.”

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:35.420
Reuters

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:36.420
And that's not all.

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:39.210
Here’s a question, and don’t google it
and cheat.

00:07:39.210 --> 00:07:47.840
Which company, BMW or Tesla do you think is
going to sell more electric cars in 2017?

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:52.000
Now many of you are probably betting on Tesla,
by a lot.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:53.000
Right?

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:55.010
Well... wait just a second..

00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:59.070
Because the truth is that, taking both electric
cars and plug-in hybrids into account, both

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:01.010
companies are actually very close.

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:07.720
And it does look like Tesla will win, but
by very little.

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:13.050
In fact, both companies are expected to close
their 2017 sales with approximately 100,000

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:14.050
electric cars.

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:18.210
Yes, okay, I'm sure some of you would argue
that Tesla has stored a lot of its Model 3

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:21.960
cars, which in principle translate into sales
for the next few years.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:27.450
“The Model 3 will be new territory for CEO
Elon Musk and Tesla as a company.

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:31.139
The sedan has already received at least 400,000
pre-orders.”

00:08:31.139 --> 00:08:32.139
Business Insider.

00:08:32.139 --> 00:08:37.349
That’s true, but the German brand also hopes
to improve its numbers.

00:08:37.349 --> 00:08:45.459
In short, as we always say here at VisualPolitik,
the future, dear viewers is by definition

00:08:45.459 --> 00:08:46.459
uncertain.

00:08:46.459 --> 00:08:49.350
Tesla could be a great company, but it won´t
be the only one.

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:53.639
The truth is that, by selling almost as many
electric cars as Tesla; by investing 5 times

00:08:53.639 --> 00:08:58.139
more in R&amp;D; and by earning a cumulative profit
of more than 30 billion dollars in the last

00:08:58.139 --> 00:09:03.500
five years, I think we can say that BMW is,
at least a very important competitor.

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:09.680
In fact, it is surprising that both companies’
market value is practically the same, considering

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:14.040
that expectations for one are so much higher
than they are for the other.

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:19.180
Especially when in recent years BMW has become
a major, and very important player in the

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:23.140
Chinese market.

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:30.670
(THE GREAT CHINESE MARKET)

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:35.350
Since 2007, and despite the international
economic crisis, the BMW group has managed,

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:41.640
in less than 10 years, to increase its number
of cars from 1,500,000 in 2007 to 2,367,000

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:43.790
cars in 2016.

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:49.019
And of course, that translates into more income
and also more benefits.

00:09:49.019 --> 00:09:58.389
See, BMW’s net benefit, that is, the money
that is left for the company after taxes,

00:09:58.389 --> 00:10:01.069
has more than doubled in this period of time.

00:10:01.069 --> 00:10:03.069
Check out this graph:

00:10:03.069 --> 00:10:13.429
Having seen it, we could say that things have
gone quite well for this company.

00:10:13.429 --> 00:10:19.160
Well... one of the pieces that has greatly
aided this progress is actually China, yes,

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:20.160
China.

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:22.410
Take a look at how their market has evolved:

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:31.160
In 2016, it managed to sell half a million
cars, out of which 300,000 were manufactured

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:36.450
in China itself (through a partnership with
a local company), and 200,000 were imported,

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:39.260
mostly from the factories that the company
has in Germany.

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:49.110
In other words, 1 out of every 4 cars sold
by the BMW group is already in China, a market

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:52.920
where the automobile sector will surge in
the upcoming years, along with its middle

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:53.920
class.

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:59.709
Well, the fact is that beyond any comparison
with Tesla, BMW's Chinese adventure shows

00:10:59.709 --> 00:11:01.129
us a couple of things:

00:11:01.129 --> 00:11:05.319
The first is that, far from what is usually
said, China could be a great source of opportunities

00:11:05.319 --> 00:11:12.050
and wealth, something which incidentally,
we have been mentioning on VisualPolitik for

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:13.050
a long time.

00:11:13.050 --> 00:11:17.069
Each year 80 million Chinese join the middle
class and that... has very clear and obvious

00:11:17.069 --> 00:11:19.110
consequences on their ability to spend.

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:23.790
Secondly, it is very common to hear politicians
of all backgrounds arguing that in order to

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:26.899
export more, the currency needs to be devalued.

00:11:26.899 --> 00:11:29.240
Well, Germany says quite the opposite.

00:11:29.240 --> 00:11:36.300
What is required isn’t a cheap currency--it’s
competitiveness and good products.

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:41.339
But we will talk about that another time.

00:11:41.339 --> 00:11:44.660
Now it’s your turn, if you had to choose,
which company would you bet on?

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:45.660
Tesla or BMW?

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:51.290
At the end of the day, as we’ve seen, both
have very a similar market value.

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:55.960
Leave your answer in the comments as well
as in the survey.

00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:59.910
I really hope you enjoyed this video, please
hit like if you did and don’t forget to

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:02.750
subscribe to our channel for brand new videos
every Monday and Thursday.

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:05.970
Also, don’t forget to check out our friends
at the Reconsider Media Podcast - they provided

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:08.360
the vocals in this episode that were not mine!

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:10.000
And as always, thanks for watching!

